    "created_at": "2016-03-17T19:39:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-17T19:39:06Z",
    "body": "The problem is the elements whose constructor does not clearly specify a tag name. E.g. `new HTMLQuoteElement()` could either be a `<q>` or a `<blockquote>`.\n\nI think at the last custom elements F2F a lot of people agreed that the best way to fix this is to just create separate interfaces for everything (so in this case `HTMLBlockquoteElement` and `HTMLQElement`, both deriving from `HTMLQuoteElement`). But I didn't quite get the sense any implementers were exciting about taking on that potential compat risk, even if we went to the trouble of speccing it. @rniwa @smaug---- @esprehn thoughts?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
