    "created_at": "2016-03-22T22:42:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-22T22:42:20Z",
    "body": "That sort of thing is fine, it's just an \"abstract class\" that cant' be directly constructed.  Not unusual.\n\nSeparately: I don't think making these constructable is very useful.  The names are very long, and the signatures are anemic.  I'd much rather have a good element-creation API that handles attr/property setting and children assigning, like every DOM library has.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
