    "created_at": "2016-03-24T17:50:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-24T17:50:39Z",
    "body": "@esprehn The issue is, you're proposing we add code to the browser to give every tagname its own interface, and make all those interfaces have a useful constructor.  Is this substantially different than _not_ doing that, and instead making a single decent element-creation function? If the code weight is anywhere near similar, the latter is _way_ more useful for authors; do you really still think we should do the former?\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
